    {
      "id": "c36626142eb61b232fe3c16a4384201ee0094e66",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2540262227,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "I think the problem here is that, if `str` is null, `xml_get_int()` returns `true` *but* doesn't set `*val*`.\n\nAccording to [the documentation page for `xmlNoteListGetString()`](https://gnome.pages.gitlab.gnome.org/libxml2/html/tree_8h.html#a98a1fa0c23bde675c65837d27aa4f5d5), it returns `NULL` if a memory allocation failed.\n\nThat should probably be treated *for now* by doing an assert of some sort for `str != NULL`, as that would print a message and abort the program - that's what GLib's memory allocator does unless it's explicitly told not to do so with a `try` call, and, if you run out of memory, you're going to have to free up a bunch of stuff to make enough memory to...\n\n...pop up a dialog that says you ran out of memory.\n\nIf you do that before calling `xml_get_int()`, it won't call `xml_get_int()` with a null pointer, so there would be no need to check for a null pointer.\n\nIf you do that *inside* `xml_get_int()`, `xml_get_int()` would not return if it were passed a null pointer, so it would never return `true` without setting `*val`.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-06-03T06:16:19.587Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-06-03T06:16:19.587Z",
